  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the clear winner so far (0.650-0.653), far exceeding singleprofile RNA (0.485-0.520) and image-only (0.208). Aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) shows negligible difference (~0.3%). The untested variable with the most potential upside is the RNA encoder: scgpt has never been tested, and as a pretrained generative model it may capture richer biological structure than scvi_n200. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting, or is scvi_n200 already near-optimal for RNA representation? This is a clean single-variable comparison against the current best (config_006), isolating the encoder effect while holding profile and aggregation fixed. Why now: With 4 experiments remaining, establishing the best RNA encoder before committing to multimodal fusion experiments ensures subsequent multimodal trials use the strongest backbone. If scgpt multiprofile matches or beats 0.653, it opens a new exploitation path; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 and can pivot remaining budget to multimodal fusion with confidence."
}

